{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNKDrugGaqUUsdN2dn2X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Triage jobs now get a fixed line such as `Worker roles: docs (network: false), engineer (network: true)` in the user message, and the report is written. The tests for the agent, agentjob and triage packages pass, and `go vet` is clean on the packages I changed.\n\nThe line is built from the resolved config in `internal/agentjob/command.go`, so every triage role gets the same text. No edit to `internal/triage/run.go` was needed. The Claude adapter in `internal/agent/claude/prompt.go` writes the line only when there is at least one worker role, so worker, reviewer and scanner messages are unchanged.\n\nI added tests in four places:\n- **Claude adapter:** the line appears with two roles (one on, one off) and is absent for an empty list.\n- **agentjob:** the triage stage gets both entries, the worker and review stages get none, and a config with no worker roles gives no error.\n- **triage:** the lead and architect roles get byte-identical lines.\n\nThe `git status` check showed only the six code and test files plus `.ard-input/299/`. The report at `.ard/299/worker-engineer.md` was written after that check.\n\nThe triage prompts under `.ard/triage/` may want to refer to the new line. Agents can't edit those files, so a person would have to."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":24987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":722},"output_tokens":414,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b1ce76b-1546-446d-ad02-184faaccb7d7","uuid":"9ad14c7d-96fc-4c34-8f01-170a55eae25a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:35:49.664Z"